       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum labeled dose, and I don't know of any indication that calls for it. It would put the patient at serious risk of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm. Because I'd be placing it directly into the system, I don't want to be the one to do that.\n\nHere's what I can do right away:\n- **Enter the maximum standard dose.** That's 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day), or 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day).\n- **Enter a lower dose.** For example, 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day), if that was the intent.\n- **Add a note to the order**, such as \"GI prophylaxis with PPI, monitor creatinine and Hgb,\" if that's useful.\n\nIf you have a specific rationale for a dose above the maximum, such as a protocol or a consult recommendation, the better route is to enter it yourself. Pharmacy can then review it and document the override. Let me know which of the options above you'd like."
